  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#47584\", \"PowerToys#48538\", \"PowerToys#48233\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before: the Command Palette dock hides when you press Win+D or click the Show Desktop button, and it comes back when you restore the windows. The closest reports are PowerToys#47584 (the original, which later reports were closed as duplicates of) and #48538, with #48233 describing the same behavior. The archive shows no fix or workaround. One maintainer could not reproduce it and wondered whether a taskbar-modifying tool such as TranslucentTB was involved, but other users saw it without any such tool. #48538 notes that the dock stayed visible while certain windows were open in the background, such as a file Properties dialog or the advanced sound settings. #48233's reporter said the behavior stopped on its own. Subscribe to #47584 for updates, and add your PowerToys and Windows versions there if they differ from those already reported.\"}",
